-- #1111 A-2.12 (#1319 unit 2) — #1283 Repro A's drain, on all three engines.
--
-- This is the shape that survived unit 1: the CONSTRUCTOR-scheme half was re-keyed
-- there, but a record literal / pattern / `.field` access never reads that env — it
-- reads `recordByNameRef`, which stayed bare-name and last-write-wins.  So Repro B
-- (the bare-ctor-member spelling) drained in unit 1 and Repro A (this one, the
-- RECORD spelling) did not.
--
-- Before: `Type mismatch: Cfg vs Cfg — … one comes from module 'armod', the other
-- from module 'zrmod'` plus `Int vs Float`, exit 1 — a diagnostic naming TWO modules
-- this file never mentions.  Measured on a binary cold-built from `main` @ 1443870c.
--
-- Hand-derived correct answer, independent of any engine: `entry` brings exactly ONE
-- `Cfg` into scope — armod's, whose `fld` is an `Int` — and `zrf 0 = 0`, so `7`.
import remod.{Cfg, mkA}
import zrmod.{zrf}

get : Cfg -> Int
get c = c.fld

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (intToString (get mkA + zrf 0))
